  "body": "## Motivation\n\nCloses #25.\n\nThe ancestry-aware intake gate added by #22 rejects the required no-rewrite synchronization path for all seven pre-law canonical-remediation PRs. Their preserved historical parent is an ancestor of current `main`, but it is outside `origin/main..HEAD`, so the validator incorrectly labels it unknown.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Seed protected-history analysis at boundary parents only when Git proves they are ancestors of the exact validated base.\n- Continue failing closed for parents outside the validated base ancestry.\n- Add a disposable-history regression that:\n  - creates a legacy canonical-remediation branch;\n  - advances protected base with grandfathered blocked intake history;\n  - merges that base into the remediation without rewriting history;\n  - proves ordinary pre-push and GitHub synthetic-merge validation both pass;\n  - proves a newly committed blocked packet still fails.\n- Carry the required deterministic `TELEMETRY.md` validation row.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node --test scripts/intake-lib.test.mjs scripts/validate-intake-package.test.mjs scripts/fail-closed.test.mjs scripts/validate-okf-provenance.test.mjs` \u2014 42 passed, 1 fixture skipped.\n- `node scripts/validate-intake.mjs --base origin/main` \u2014 clean.\n- `node scripts/validate-okf.mjs` \u2014 2,611 files clean; index fresh.\n- `node --test scripts/validate-okf-visuals.test.mjs` \u2014 5 passed.\n- `node .claude/hooks/okf-guard.mjs self-test` \u2014 green.\n- Exact PR #19 local no-rewrite merge witness `01efceb41ab9eb22f03deaa941691e6f88050137`, with the patched validator and base `c471bf43f97edfa60aa781a69248e5aa5af4c6ce` \u2014 `validate-intake: clean`.\n\n## Risk and audit gate\n\nThis changes a fail-closed history boundary. Do not merge on CI alone. Require a fresh independent exact-head PASS that confirms:\n\n1. only true ancestors of the exact base are accepted as legacy boundary roots;\n2. unknown parents still fail closed;\n3. ordinary and synthetic legacy-sync paths agree;\n4. mutate/restore, add/delete, rename-out, partial canonical writes, and newly committed blocked packets remain rejected.\n\nMerge method must be a merge commit; squash and rebase remain disabled.\n",
